# The pinned Closure Compiler release: the one place that names the oracle
# jar. The oracle and bench tooling read this file (tools/oracle/fetch.sh and
# build.sh, tools/clie2e/build-java.sh and main.go, tools/bench/bench.py), so
# pointing every Java tool at another jar is a change of CLOSURE_JAR here.
# Plain KEY=value lines: shell scripts source it, the Go and Python tools
# parse it.
#
# CLOSURE_VERSION     the release tag. The Go port's own copies of it are
#                     CommandLineRunnerVersion_COMPILER_VERSION
#                     (internal/jscomp/command_line_runner_version.go) and
#                     tag in tools/licenses/main.go; their tests check that
#                     they agree with this file.
# CLOSURE_JAR         the oracle jar: a file name in the .cache/ directory
#                     the tool uses (the main checkout's, shared by all
#                     worktrees, unless the tool says otherwise).
# CLOSURE_JAR_SHA256  the sha256 digests that fetch.sh accepts for it,
#                     space-separated: Maven Central's
#                     closure-compiler-$CLOSURE_VERSION.jar, which fetch.sh
#                     downloads when the jar is missing. Only Maven's jar
#                     shades the bundled libraries under
#                     com.google.javascript.jscomp.jarjar, as the jar of every
#                     earlier pin did; the npm build of the same release
#                     (google-closure-compiler-java, compiler.jar) holds the
#                     same Closure classes and resources unshaded, so the
#                     oracle tools that import shaded classes do not compile
#                     against it, and it is not accepted.
# CLOSURE_SRC_SHA256  the sha256 digest of Maven Central's
#                     closure-compiler-$CLOSURE_VERSION-sources.jar, which
#                     fetch.sh downloads as .cache/closure-src.jar and unpacks
#                     into .cache/closure-src.
#
# Moving the pin (tools/oracle/README.md, "Moving the pin"): change
# CLOSURE_VERSION, CLOSURE_JAR_SHA256 and CLOSURE_SRC_SHA256, and either point
# CLOSURE_JAR at the new jar or delete the old .cache/$CLOSURE_JAR so that
# fetch.sh fetches the new one; replace .cache/closure-src with the new
# sources (fetch.sh does it when they are missing).
CLOSURE_VERSION=v20261021
CLOSURE_JAR=closure-compiler-v20261021-maven.jar
CLOSURE_JAR_SHA256="8a0d71ccce8ab78afe8c3cee130cda3af4178a6732435982815a37738ad9078a"
CLOSURE_SRC_SHA256="63b47d79f92db491a14f02e2609e6331d383cb3da27e4031db7d8f1083e22658"
